arch/index/mapper/FieldMapper.java-DST-ADDITION-26154-26214-MethodDeclaration","path":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/FieldMapper.java","srcDst":"DST","content":"public boolean isSet() {\n            return isSet;\n        }","nodeType":"ADDITION","treeType":"MethodDeclaration","descendantSimpleNames":["isSet","isSet"],"identifiers":["isSet"],"startLine":681,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":683,"endLineOffset":9,"length":61,"subs":[]}]},{"comment":"The deletion of `List.of(...)` and subsequent addition with new invalid examples introduces a discrepancy in how invalid configurations are handled. The addition of `b.field(\"store\", \"false\")` in invalid examples sets the store attribute as a string instead of a boolean.  \n[Symptom] -\u003e [Technical Cause] -\u003e [Systemic Risk]: The original code used `List.of` to create an immutable list of invalid examples, and the new code uses the same method but includes additional examples set as strings -\u003e Incomplete test coverage for edge cases and type mismatch -\u003e Potential bugs or misconfigurations that pass validation, leading to runtime exceptions or incorrect behavior.","nodes":[{"id":"server/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/TextFieldMapperTests.java-SRC-DELETION-58341-58345-METHOD_INVOCATION_RECEIVER","path":"server/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/TextFieldMapperTests.java","srcDst":"SRC","content":"List","nodeType":"DELETION","treeType":"METHOD_INVOCATION_RECEIVER","descendantSimpleNames":["List"],"startLine":1177,"startLineOffset":23,"endLine":1177,"endLineOffset":27,"length":5,"subs":[]},{"id":"server/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/TextFieldMapperTests.java-DST-ADDITION-58531-58533-SimpleName","path":"server/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/TextFieldMapperTests.java","srcDst":"DST","content":"of","nodeType":"ADDITION","treeType":"SimpleName","descendantSimpleNames":["of"],"startLine":1181,"startLineOffset":28,"endLine":1181,"endLineOff